# =============================================================================
# smoke_test/.env.example  —  copy to smoke_test/.env and edit, OR just export
# these vars before running test.sh. Every value has a sensible default, so the
# file is OPTIONAL; you only need it to override the target or OTP recovery.
#
#   cp smoke_test/.env.example smoke_test/.env
#   vim smoke_test/.env
# =============================================================================

# --- target ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL of the auth service. On the deploy box the service is published on
# host port 10001 (10001 -> container 8000). Run this test ON the box (or via an
# SSH tunnel); your laptop usually cannot reach :10001 directly (security group).
#   on the box:        http://3.109.183.124:10001
#   inside container:  http://3.109.183.124:8000
#   via API gateway:   http://3.109.183.124:10015   (gateway rewrites /api/v1/auth/*)
AUTH_URL=http://3.109.183.124:10001

# --- bootstrap ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The seeded platform admin phone (config DEFAULT_ADMIN_PHONE). The test logs in
# as this admin to exercise the RBAC + KYC-review suites. Must match the auth
# service's configured value.
ADMIN_PHONE=01700000000

# --- OTP recovery via the support service (PREFERRED) ------------------------
# The 00-support service consumes auth's OTP queue and exposes the codes over
# HTTP (GET /otp/latest?phone=…). The harness reads codes from it — no docker or
# SSH access required, and it works from a laptop. Falls back to docker/SSH if
# unreachable. On the box, the default http://3.109.183.124:10099 is correct.
SUPPORT_URL=http://3.109.183.124:10099

# --- OTP recovery fallback (docker logs / SSH) -------------------------------
# OTP is currently ENABLED, so /verify needs the real 6-digit code. In dev the
# code is logged ("[DEV-OTP] phone=.. purpose=.. code=..") and the harness
# recovers it from the container's logs.
#   * ON THE BOX: local `docker logs $AUTH_CONTAINER` is used automatically.
#   * FROM A LAPTOP: set AUTH_SSH + AUTH_SSH_KEY so codes are pulled over SSH.
AUTH_CONTAINER=dokandar_auth_service_dev
# AUTH_SSH=ubuntu@3.109.183.124
# AUTH_SSH_KEY=/home/jakir/Desktop/DevOps/mumbai-key.pem

# --- admin OTP rate-limit reset ----------------------------------------------
# The seeded admin phone is reused every run; OTP_RATE_PER_HOUR (=5) would
# throttle admin login after a few reruns. The harness clears the admin's
# per-phone OTP rate key at startup. It auto-reads the redis URL from
# ../env/.env.dev when run inside the repo; override here if needed.
# REDIS_RESET_URL=redis://:<password>@172.31.12.210:6379/0

# --- harness knobs -----------------------------------------------------------
# per-request curl timeout, seconds (keep comments on their OWN line, not inline)
TIMEOUT=15
# OUTPUT_DIR=./smoke_test/out
# RESULT_JSON=./smoke_test/out/result.json
# LOG_FILE=./smoke_test/out/smoke.log
# NO_COLOR=1

# =============================================================================
# Cross-service note (per the platform convention of taking peer endpoints from
# env): the AUTH service has NO synchronous HTTP dependency on any other service.
# It emits domain events via a transactional outbox -> Kafka, and it SERVES
# /jwks + a gRPC API that OTHER services consume to verify its JWTs. So there are
# no outbound peer URLs to configure for auth's own tests. The variables below
# are accepted-but-unused, present only for fleet-wide .env uniformity.
# =============================================================================
# 01_AUTH_HOST=172.17.0.1
# 01_AUTH_PORT=10001
# 15_API_GATEWAY_HOST=172.17.0.1
# 15_API_GATEWAY_PORT=10015
